   "note": "'Rabies spreads primarily through bites or scratches from an infected animal.' 'The rabies virus must travel to the brain before it can cause symptoms.' Treatment after exposure is 'nearly 100% effective if you get it after exposure'. 'Once clinical signs of rabies appear, the disease is nearly always fatal.'"
  }
